  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Specific Somanathapura Chennakesava standing temple: three stellate stone shrine towers/walls, stepped shared jagati platform, low east-facing mandapa and recessed doorway, original simplified figure/niche/miniature-shrine/frieze vocabulary, patterned receding tower registers and domical caps/finials. Picture-led approximate low enclosing open pillared corridor, east entrance pavilion/short stairs and separate plain stone pillar. Existing shared stone/material graphs; no copied narrative/deity/text atlas, full ritual interior or broad courtyard ground slab.",
    "identityBasis": "Named standard PMTiles Keshava Temple archaeological-site point35184523899922 correlates the main lobed building35184523899920. No exact-QID building attribution claimed. Anchor76.88155573,12.27573677; heading0, internal local+x angle-.13rad, entrance approximately east/local+x. Three lobe centers establish west/north/south shrine stations; the eastern lobe establishes the mandapa. Standard map does not resolve the enclosing corridor: its68x52m approximate picture-led footprint is fitted to open surroundings and the east footway, with no mapped dimension claim. Native toilet point and remote independent building stay outside it.",
    "heightBasis": "Ordinary-picture/map visualization estimates, not survey dimensions: main mapped envelope about31x25m, three shrine centers in west/north/south lobes, approximately8.4m shrine width,1.15m jagati, temple eaves6.2m, four receding tower registers to10.3m, domical caps/finials to11.5m above the local base. Mandapa roof about6.2m and low central crest7.1m. Enclosure about68x52m with4.4m-deep open corridors,3.4m columns/eaves, separate4.5m-high gate pavilion and approximately8m plain pillar. Hidden layout, sculptural counts, damage and exact thresholds remain approximate.",
    "terrainBasis": "Retain original standard6m Mapzen ground, water and all independent buildings. Main jagati is locally level with buried bottom edges and short east stairs; enclosure outer walls/column footings and roof ranges follow sampled native grade. Court stays native ground. No broad courtyard/plaza slab, flattening or ground/water cutout. Coarse rural DEM does not resolve stone paving, thresholds or exact court elevation; picture-led enclosure dimensions and absolute heights remain approximate.",
